# Git commands after each change

The user runs git themselves. Whenever you finish a batch of code/test/rule changes (not mid-exploration), end with **copy-paste command blocks**.

## Always include (Windows / this PC)

PowerShell-friendly, from the repo root:

```powershell
git add -A
git status
git commit -m "Short imperative subject"
git push
```

- Subject: one line, ~50–72 chars, imperative, why-focused, no trailing period
- Do **not** run these unless they explicitly ask you to commit/push

## Include Linux when the change needs the CreoPDM host

If the fix is served by the Linux CreoPDM service (API, `app.js`, templates, settings, etc.), also give:

```bash
git pull
systemctl --user restart creopdm.service
```

Skip the Linux block for docs-only, rules-only, or pure Windows-agent work that does not need a server restart.

## Example

```text
Windows (commit + push):
git add -A
git status
git commit -m "Disable check-in comment when nothing to submit"
git push

Linux (deploy):
git pull
systemctl --user restart creopdm.service
```
